#DESCRIPTION
Full PIC (kinetic ions AND kinetic electrons) parallel whistler-Alfven wave
test. The standard Maxwell/GMRES field solver advances E and B; both ion and
electron species are kinetic, so this exercises the full electromagnetic PIC
dispersion (electron + ion contributions).

Same geometry/normalization/seed as the hybrid variant (PARAM.in.hybrid): in
code units d_i ~ v_A ~ B = Omega_i ~ 1 and box Lx = 6.4 d_i, so the n=1 mode
sits at k d_i ~ 1.  NOTE the two variants do NOT measure the same branch here:
the decks set cLight = uNormSI, which with d_i ~ 1 gives c/v_A ~ 0.98, so the
displacement current is not negligible and the full-EM R-mode is well below
the Hall whistler.  For k d_i = 0.982 the full cold-plasma root (c = 1,
m_i/m_e = 1836, n_e = n_i) is omega/Omega_i = 0.786, i.e. period T = 8.0 s,
while the hybrid variant measures the massless-electron Hall value 1.58.  The
two kinetic species are ions (q = m = 1) and electrons (q = -1, m = 1/1836).

#INITFROMSWMF
F                       initFromSWMF

#GEOMETRY
-3.2                    xMin  [code units; Lx = 6.4 d_i]
 3.2                    xMax
-0.05                   yMin
 0.05                   yMax
-0.05                   zMin
 0.05                   zMax

#NCELL
64                      nCellX
1                       nCellY
1                       nCellZ

#MAXBLOCKSIZE
64                      maxBlockSizeX
1                       maxBlockSizeY
1                       maxBlockSizeZ

#PERIODICITY
T                       isPeriodicX
T                       isPeriodicY
T                       isPeriodicZ

#SOLVEEM
T                       solveEM

Two kinetic species: ions (q = 1, m = 1) and electrons (q = -1, m = 1/1836).
The electron is kinetic here (unlike the hybrid variant where it is a fluid),
so the PIC Maxwell solve carries the full whistler dispersion.
#PLASMA
2                       nS
1.0                     mass           Species 0: ions
1.0                     charge
1.0/1836.0              mass           Species 1: electrons
-1.0                    charge

#UNIFORMSTATE
5.0                     rho [amu/cc]   Species 0: ions (n = 5 /cc)
0.0                     ux [km/s]
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
10000.0                 T [K]          ~ ions, code T ~ 0.2 (T_code = k_B T/uNorm^2)
2.7233e-3               rho [amu/cc]   Species 1: electrons (n_e = n_i = 5 /cc)
0.0                     ux [km/s]
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
5.4574                  T [K]          ~ electrons, code T ~ 0.2 (same T_code as ions)
1.0439e-8               bx [T]       uniform guide field Bx0 (B_code ~ 1)
0.0                     by [T]
0.0                     bz [T]
0.0                     ex [V/m]
0.0                     ey [V/m]
0.0                     ez [V/m]

Same transverse circularly-polarized right-hand seed (frac = 0.02) and Alfven
velocity kick as the hybrid variant, applied to both species.
#TESTCASE
HybridWave

#WAVEIC
T                       rightHand      right-hand (whistler) helicity
1                       waveMode       box-fundamental (n=1) mode

#TIMESTEPPING
T                       useFixedDt
0.02                    dt

#NORMALIZATION
1.0e5                   lNormSI   [m]  ~ d_i so d_i ~ 1 in code units
1.0e5                   uNormSI   [m/s] tNorm = 1 s; sets cLight_SI = uNormSI

#MONITOR
50                      dnReport

#SAVELOG
10                      dnSavePic
10                      dnSavePT

#PARTICLES
250                     nParticle per cell in X
1                       nParticle per cell in Y
1                       nParticle per cell in Z

#SAVEPLOT
1                       nPlot
z=0 fluid ascii pic     plotString
10                      dn
-1                      dt
1                       dx

#STOP
-1                      MaxIter
24.0                    TimeMax   ~3 full-EM whistler periods (T = 8.0 s here)

#RUN
